<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/10th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sviatoslav's invasion of Bulgaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/968">968</a>–<a href="/years/971">971</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sviatoslav-i-of-kiev">Sviatoslav</a>'s invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> was the campaign of 968–971 in which Sviatoslav I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a>, first invited by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a>, conquered much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-bulgarian-empire">First Bulgarian Empire</a> and settled at Pereyaslavets on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>. The Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-tzimiskes">John I Tzimiskes</a> then drove him out, besieging him at Dorostolon in 971; Sviatoslav was killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pechenegs">Pechenegs</a> on his way home in 972.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sviatoslavs-invasion-of-bulgaria.jpg" alt="Sviatoslav's invasion of Bulgaria" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Constantine Manasses · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:63-manasses-chronicle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
